The frame is shared too:
• The same track. Both modes draw the 14 cells of the same Board, tapped one at a time.
• The same loop. Each cell opens one modal card with one sentence, one answer and one verdict, then closes.
• The same balance. Both modes split the 14 cells into 7 "recognise" and 7 "produce".
• The same marking. Typed answers in Game go through the exam's own normalising, so a Game cell is marked exactly like an exam question.
What Game adds is a costume and some pressure: three lives, a score, a clock inside Defuse, another try after a mistake, and the cup for a clean run. So the gap to close is not the sentences any more. It is the shape of the experience: one sentence, one answer, fourteen times.
Every game in the repository
The repository holds about 40 games. Almost all of them are a pick-one, pair, sort or type decision on one item at a time. What varies is the stage around the decision: falling cards, drifting words, wires, pendulums, a boss.
Live: linked from a menu or a topic's header. Unused: finished and loading, but not linked. Broken: fails to load.
